@startuml hil_lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam arrowColor #6366F1
skinparam noteBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

title k9x HIL — Lifecycle Flow\nDesign → Configure → Implement → Runtime

|#EEF2FF| Architect (Studio) |
start
:Architect opens **k9x Studio**;
:Designs agentic workflow on canvas;
:Identifies decision points requiring\nhuman judgment (**Discernment**);
:Drops **HIL Orchestrator** from palette;
note right
  Studio suggests where HIL
  is needed based on 4Ds analysis.
  Architect can move, delete,
  or override suggestions.
end note
:Defines HIL topics on canvas\ne.g. workflow.hil.{project}.{app}.{queue};
:Generates scaffold with\n**BaseHILOrchestrator** wired in;

|#FEF3C7| Admin (k9x-HIL Platform) |
:Admin logs into **k9x-HIL** admin panel;
:Creates **Project**;
:Registers **Application(s)** under Project;
:Defines **Queues** per Application\nwith Kafka topic mappings;
note right
  Queue = Kafka topic (1:1)
  workflow.hil.eoc.claims.document-review
  workflow.hil.eoc.claims.escalations
end note
:Assigns **Users/Groups** to Applications\n(IAM: who sees what);
:Sets policies per Queue\n- TTL, default action on expiry\n- PII handling rules\n- Required role/group;

|#D1FAE5| Solutions Architect (Implementation) |
:SA takes scaffold from Studio;
:Implements agent business logic;
:Wires orchestrator to publish to\nKafka HIL topics matching admin config;
:Configures **reply_to** topic\nfor response routing;
:Implements **HILOrchestrator**\nsubscribing to response topic;
note right
  Inbound message schema:
  - correlation_id, reply_to
  - title, description, priority
  - ttl_hours, ttl_action
  - pii, pii_fields
  - payload, artifacts
  - required_role, required_group
end note
:Deploys to runtime environment;

|#E0E7FF| Runtime (k9x-HIL + Kafka) |
:Agent executes, reaches HIL gate;
:Orchestrator publishes task to\n**workflow.hil.{project}.{app}.{queue}**;
:k9x-HIL consumer picks up message;
:Task created, routed to correct\nProject → Application → Queue;
:Task assigned to user/group\n(auto or pool-based);

|#FEF3C7| Worker (k9x-HIL UI) |
:Worker logs in;
:Sees Application tabs with\nassigned tasks;
:Opens task — views description,\npayload, artifacts;
if (PII flagged?) then (yes)
  :Masked fields shown\nAudit log on view;
else (no)
endif
:Reviews, adds comments;

if (Decision?) then (Complete)
  :Provides decision + comment;
  :Status → **completed**;
elseif (Escalate) then
  :Escalates to manager;
  :Status → **escalated**;
elseif (Reject) then
  :Rejects with reason;
  :Status → **rejected**;
else (No action — TTL expires)
  :System performs **ttl_action**\n(reject / approve / escalate / expire);
  note right
    auto: true in response
    so caller knows it was
    a timeout, not human
  end note
endif

|#E0E7FF| Runtime (k9x-HIL + Kafka) |
:k9x-HIL publishes response to\n**reply_to** topic;
note right
  Response schema:
  - correlation_id, task_id
  - action, actor, auto
  - decision, comment
  - completed_at
end note
:HILOrchestrator consumes response;
:Resumes downstream agents\nwith human decision in context;

stop

legend right
  **k9x HIL — Roles**
  Architect: Designs where HIL happens (Studio)
  Admin: Configures projects, apps, queues, IAM
  SA: Implements and wires Kafka topics
  Worker: Performs human tasks at runtime
  ----
  **Principles**
  - Event-driven, fully decoupled
  - Topic = Queue (1:1 mapping)
  - Caller owns the contract (schema in message)
  - Framework-agnostic (any Kafka producer)
  - TTL enforced, PII-aware, audit-logged
endlegend

@enduml
